% Linux Libertine, matching the WikiPathways website's house style (see
% WP_HOUSE_STYLE.md and wikipathways.github.io/style.md), scoped to
% \wpheadingfont rather than made the document default: used only for the
% front-page "WikiPathways News" masthead and article/editorial titles
% (\WPnews@chapter above). Loaded via the CTAN `libertine` package, i.e.
% resolved by name through TeX Live's own font database, rather than by
% an explicit file path to a vendored copy: the latter (tried first, for
% both Linux Libertine and Poppins) made lualatex intermittently fail to
% embed the font once this newsletter's articles are all combined into
% one document - see RESTYLING.md.
\RequirePackage{libertine}
\newcommand{\wpheadingfont}{\libertine}
